        <headline>Beach Hazards Statement issued September 26 at 1:40AM CDT until September 26 at 10:00PM CDT by NWS Duluth MN</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Dangerous swimming conditions are expected along the
Lake Superior shoreline due to high wave action and strong rip
currents.

* WHERE...Minnesota Park Point and Wisconsin Point Beaches.

* WHEN...From noon CDT today through this evening.

* IMPACTS...Life-threatening waves and rip currents are expected.
Stay out of the water and stay away from dangerous areas like
piers and breakwalls.
</description>
        <instruction>Remain out of the water to avoid hazardous swimming conditions.</instruction>
